course: dictionary
lesson: 11057
title: Weekdays and weekends
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A weekday is any day of the week except Saturday and Sunday: Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday or Friday. Read the words around it to check. «Most grown-ups spend about a third of their weekdays at work» tells you weekdays are the days when most people work, not the weekend.
explain: Weekday can be a noun, an adjective or an adverb. In «a weekday morning», weekday describes the morning, so it is an adjective. In «the shop opens at nine weekdays», it tells you when, so it is an adverb meaning on weekdays. Always ask: what does the word do in this sentence?
explain: Numbers in the sentences help too. «The week is a merry-go-round of 7 seats» shows that a week has 7 days. Two of those days are the weekend, so the weekdays must be the other 5. That is a clue to the meaning, and you can check it with a calendar.
fact: A weekday is any day from Monday to Friday.
fact: A week has 5 weekdays and 2 weekend days, so two whole weeks have 10 weekdays.
fact: «Weekday» can be a noun («a weekday»), an adjective («a weekday timetable») or used as «weekdays» to mean on weekdays.
fact: Many weekday names come from the sky: «Sunday» from the Sun, «Monday» from the Moon, and «Saturday» from the planet Saturn.
fact: «1 January 2000 was a Saturday», and phones and computers use calendar rules to find the weekday of any date.
exercise: How many weekdays are there in one week? | *5 | 7 | 2 | 10
exercise: Which of these is a weekday? | Sunday | Saturday | Weekend | *Wednesday
exercise: Ella says weekday means any day of the week. Is she right? | Yes, every day is a weekday | No, weekdays are only Saturday and Sunday | Weekdays are only the days in summer | *Not quite, weekdays are Monday to Friday
test: In «a weekday timetable», what kind of word is weekday? | adverb | verb | *adjective | noun
test: How many weekdays are there in two weeks? | 14 | 5 | *10 | 7
exam: Which day is NOT a weekday? | Friday | *Sunday | Tuesday | Monday
